IMPORT prelude

-- Visiting Forces Act 1960 (Singapore) -- who counts as connected with a visiting force (ss 2, 4, 5), whose service courts may
-- exercise jurisdiction here (s 6), when a Singapore prosecution may go ahead (s 7), custody after arrest (s 9), claims the courts
-- will not hear (s 10), death inquiries and removal of bodies (s 11), the weight of certificates (ss 14, 16, 18), deserters (s 15)
-- and attachment of Singapore personnel (s 17).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/VFA1960.txt. The deposit says
-- it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; no later
-- amendment is annotated in the text.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions with decision content
-- for a person, a police officer, a prosecutor, a coroner or a court. Not encoded: the President's orders designating countries and
-- modifying the Act (s 3), the power to extend Singapore-forces law to visiting forces (s 12), claims settlement arrangements (s 13),
-- the passport presumptions (s 14(3)), mutual powers of command (s 17(2)-(4)) and the identity presumptions of s 18(2), (3). Which
-- countries are designated, and what any treaty says about primary jurisdiction, lies outside the deposit.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Visiting Forces Act 1960`

§§ `2 -- dependants and reservists`

-- s 2(1): "dependant", in relation to a member of a force or civilian component, means a person who is "not ordinarily resident in
-- Singapore" and who is (a) the wife or husband of any such member; (b) wholly or mainly maintained or employed by any such member;
-- or (c) in the custody, charge or care, or forms part of the family, of any such member.
-- s 2(5): time spent in Singapore as a member, civilian or dependant does not count towards ordinary residence.
GIVEN `ordinarily resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `spouse of the member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `wholly or mainly maintained or employed by the member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in the member's care or part of the family` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a dependant` IF
        (NOT `ordinarily resident in Singapore`)
    AND (    `spouse of the member`
          OR `wholly or mainly maintained or employed by the member`
          OR `in the member's care or part of the family`)

-- s 2(2): a member of a reserve or auxiliary force is deemed a member of that country's forces "so long as, but only so long as, he
-- is called into actual service ... or is called out for training".
GIVEN `called into actual service` IS A BOOLEAN, `called out for training` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reservist counts as a member` IF
    `called into actual service` OR `called out for training`

§§ `4 -- member of a civilian component (Part 2)`

-- s 4(1): a person "for the time being fulfilling all the following conditions": (a) holds a passport issued by a government, "not
-- being a passport issued by the passport authorities of Singapore"; (b) the passport contains an uncancelled entry by the
-- appropriate authority of the sending country stating that he is a member of a civilian component; (c) the passport contains a
-- note of recognition of that entry by the Minister for immigration "which has not been cancelled and as respects which no
-- notification in writing has been given ... stating that the recognition is withdrawn".
GIVEN `holds a non-Singapore passport` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `passport has an uncancelled sending-country entry` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `passport has a note of recognition` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `recognition cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `withdrawal of recognition notified in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a member of a civilian component` IF
        `holds a non-Singapore passport`
    AND `passport has an uncancelled sending-country entry`
    AND `passport has a note of recognition`
    AND (NOT `recognition cancelled`)
    AND (NOT `withdrawal of recognition notified in writing`)

§§ `5 -- relevant association (Part 2)`

-- s 5: a relevant association means being (a) "a member of that visiting force or a member of a civilian component of that force";
-- or (b) "a person (not being a citizen of Singapore or ordinarily resident in Singapore) being a dependant" of such a member.
DECLARE Connection IS ONE OF
    `a member of the visiting force`
    `a member of its civilian component`
    `a dependant of a member`
    `no connection`

GIVEN `the connection` IS A Connection, `citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `ordinarily resident here` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a relevant association` IF
    CONSIDER `the connection`
    WHEN `a member of the visiting force` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a member of its civilian component` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a dependant of a member` THEN (NOT `citizen of Singapore`) AND (NOT `ordinarily resident here`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6 -- service courts sitting in Singapore`

-- s 6(1): the service courts and service authorities of a designated country "may within Singapore ... exercise over persons subject
-- to their jurisdiction ... all such powers as are exercisable by them according to the law of that country".
-- s 6(2): those persons are (a) "members of any visiting force of that country"; (b) persons "not being citizens of Singapore"
-- seconded or attached to the Singapore Armed Forces under a treaty, whose terms of service subject them to that jurisdiction; and
-- (c) all other persons "being neither citizens of Singapore nor ordinarily resident in Singapore" subject to that country's service
-- law otherwise than as members. Proviso: a person is NOT treated as a member of a visiting force if he became (or last became) a
-- member "at a time when he was in Singapore, unless it is shown that he then became a member of those forces with his consent".
-- Paragraph (a) carries no citizenship condition.
DECLARE ServiceStatus IS ONE OF
    `serving in the visiting force`
    `attached to the Singapore Armed Forces under a treaty`
    `otherwise subject to the service law`
    `not subject to the service law`

GIVEN `the status` IS A ServiceStatus,
      `a Singapore citizen` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `ordinarily resident` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `joined the force while in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `consent to joining shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is subject to the service courts' jurisdiction` IF
    CONSIDER `the status`
    WHEN `serving in the visiting force` THEN NOT (`joined the force while in Singapore` AND (NOT `consent to joining shown`))
    WHEN `attached to the Singapore Armed Forces under a treaty` THEN NOT `a Singapore citizen`
    WHEN `otherwise subject to the service law` THEN (NOT `a Singapore citizen`) AND (NOT `ordinarily resident`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 6(4): "a sentence of death passed by a service court ... shall not be carried out in Singapore unless under the law of Singapore
-- a sentence of death could have been passed in a similar case."
GIVEN `Singapore law could have imposed death in a similar case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a service court death sentence may be carried out in Singapore` IF
    `Singapore law could have imposed death in a similar case`

§§ `7 -- prosecution in a Singapore court`

-- s 7(1): "No prosecution for an offence alleged to have been committed by a member of a visiting force shall be instituted in any
-- court of Singapore unless" the Public Prosecutor certifies either (a) that Singapore has exclusive or primary jurisdiction under a
-- treaty and has not waived it; or (b) that the service authorities have the primary right but it has been waived by them or by
-- their government. s 14(6): the certificate is "conclusive evidence of the facts stated therein".
DECLARE PrimaryRight IS ONE OF
    `Singapore has exclusive or primary jurisdiction`
    `the service authorities have primary jurisdiction`

GIVEN `who holds the right` IS A PrimaryRight, `Singapore waived` IS A BOOLEAN, `the service side waived` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Public Prosecutor can certify` IF
    CONSIDER `who holds the right`
    WHEN `Singapore has exclusive or primary jurisdiction` THEN NOT `Singapore waived`
    WHEN `the service authorities have primary jurisdiction` THEN `the service side waived`

-- s 7(2): a person tried by a service court under s 6(1) powers duly exercised under a treaty "shall not be tried for the same
-- offence by any court of Singapore". s 7(3): the President may extend s 7(1) by order to other persons with a relevant association.
-- s 7(4): arrest, warrant and remand may proceed without a certificate, "but the case shall not be further prosecuted until such a
-- certificate has been given".
GIVEN `a member of a visiting force` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `brought within s 7(1) by Presidential order` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Public Prosecutor has certified` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `already tried by a service court for the same offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Singapore prosecution may proceed` IF
        (NOT `already tried by a service court for the same offence`)
    AND (    `the Public Prosecutor has certified`
          OR (     (NOT `a member of a visiting force`)
               AND (NOT `brought within s 7(1) by Presidential order`)))

§§ `9 -- custody after arrest by the police`

-- s 9(2): where a person to whom the section applies is taken into custody by a police officer and not released, and (a) "it is
-- apparent that he has a relevant association with a visiting force", he "shall as soon as practicable thereafter, be delivered or
-- remanded into the custody of a service authority"; or (b) it is not apparent but there are reasonable grounds for believing that he
-- is subject to the service courts' jurisdiction, "he may be detained in custody for a period not exceeding 24 hours; but if within
-- that period he is not delivered into the custody of a service authority ... he shall be released on bail or brought before a
-- Magistrate".
DECLARE CustodyOutcome IS ONE OF
    `deliver to the service authority as soon as practicable`
    `may hold up to 24 hours to decide`
    `ordinary Singapore procedure`

GIVEN `association apparent` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonable grounds to believe subject to service courts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A CustodyOutcome
DECIDE `what the police do with the arrested person` IS
    IF `association apparent`
    THEN `deliver to the service authority as soon as practicable`
    ELSE IF `reasonable grounds to believe subject to service courts`
         THEN `may hold up to 24 hours to decide`
         ELSE `ordinary Singapore procedure`

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum hours of holding to decide` IS 24

GIVEN `hours held` IS A NUMBER, `delivered to the service authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must now be bailed or brought before a Magistrate` IF
    (NOT `delivered to the service authority`) AND `hours held` > `the maximum hours of holding to decide`

§§ `10 -- claims the Singapore courts will not entertain`

-- s 10: "No proceedings shall be entertained by any court of Singapore with regard to the pay of any person in respect of service as a
-- member of a visiting force or as a member of a civilian component of such a force, with regard to the terms of such service or with
-- regard to a person's discharge from such service."
DECLARE ClaimSubject IS ONE OF
    `pay for service with the force`
    `the terms of that service`
    `discharge from that service`
    `injury in a road accident`
    `an unpaid private debt`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A ClaimSubject
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Singapore court may entertain the claim` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `pay for service with the force` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the terms of that service` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `discharge from that service` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `11 -- death inquiries and removal of bodies`

-- s 11(1): if the Magistrate or Coroner is satisfied the deceased had a relevant association with a visiting force, "then unless the
-- Minister otherwise directs" he "shall not hold the inquiry or, if the inquiry has been begun but not completed, shall adjourn" it.
-- s 11(2): likewise, unless the Minister otherwise directs, he shall adjourn if a person subject to the service courts "has been charged
-- before a court of that country with causing the death", or is being detained with a view to being so charged.
GIVEN `deceased had a relevant association` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `someone charged before a service court with causing the death` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `someone detained with a view to such a charge` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the inquiry must not proceed` IF
        (NOT `the Minister directs otherwise`)
    AND (    `deceased had a relevant association`
          OR `someone charged before a service court with causing the death`
          OR `someone detained with a view to such a charge`)

-- s 11(4): any law restricting removal of a body out of Singapore "shall not apply to the body of a person who at the time of his death
-- had a relevant association with a visiting force"; (5) except where, by a Minister's direction under (1) or (3), an inquiry is
-- required to be held or resumed.
GIVEN `the deceased had a relevant association` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister has required an inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body may be removed free of the usual restrictions` IF
    `the deceased had a relevant association` AND (NOT `the Minister has required an inquiry`)

§§ `14, 16, 18 -- what certificates prove`

-- s 14(1): an appropriate authority's certificate that a person was or was not a member of a visiting force is "sufficient evidence ...
-- unless the contrary is proved". s 14(2): a certificate of a service court sentence, of detention, or of trial is "conclusive evidence".
-- s 14(4): a passport entry that a person is a dependant is "sufficient evidence ... unless the contrary is proved". s 14(5): a
-- certificate that an alleged offence "arose out of and in the course of his duty" is "sufficient evidence ... unless the contrary is
-- proved". s 14(6): the Public Prosecutor's s 7(1) certificate is "conclusive evidence". s 16(b): a commanding officer's certificate that a
-- person is a deserter or absentee is "sufficient evidence, unless the contrary is proved". s 18(1)(a): a certificate that a body of forces
-- is or was present in Singapore is "conclusive evidence".
DECLARE Certificate IS ONE OF
    `membership of a visiting force`
    `a service court sentence, detention or trial`
    `a passport entry naming a dependant`
    `an offence arising in the course of duty`
    `the Public Prosecutor's section 7 certificate`
    `a deserter or absentee`
    `presence of the force in Singapore`

DECLARE Weight IS ONE OF
    `conclusive`
    `sufficient unless the contrary is proved`

GIVEN `the certificate` IS A Certificate
GIVETH A Weight
DECIDE `the weight of the certificate` IS
    CONSIDER `the certificate`
    WHEN `a service court sentence, detention or trial` THEN `conclusive`
    WHEN `the Public Prosecutor's section 7 certificate` THEN `conclusive`
    WHEN `presence of the force in Singapore` THEN `conclusive`
    OTHERWISE `sufficient unless the contrary is proved`

§§ `15 -- deserters from a foreign force`

-- s 15(1): the Singapore Armed Forces Act 1972 provisions on apprehending deserters and absentees "apply in relation to deserters and
-- absentees without leave from the forces of any country to which this section applies"; (2) the powers "shall not be exercised in
-- relation to a person except in compliance with a request (whether specific or general) of the appropriate authority of the country to
-- which he belongs".
GIVEN `the country is designated for s 15` IS A BOOLEAN, `its appropriate authority has requested` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deserter may be apprehended` IF
    `the country is designated for s 15` AND `its appropriate authority has requested`

§§ `17 -- lending Singapore personnel to a foreign force`

-- s 17(1)(b): the Armed Forces Council, "subject to anything to the contrary in the conditions applicable to his service", may place a
-- member of a Singapore force at the disposal of a designated country's service authorities, "except that the power ... shall not be
-- exercisable in relation to any person without his consent".
GIVEN `the member consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `conditions of service forbid it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Singapore serviceman may be placed at a foreign force's disposal` IF
    `the member consents` AND (NOT `conditions of service forbid it`)

-- s 17(5): forces are deemed to be serving together or acting in combination "if and only if they are declared to be so serving or so
-- acting by order of the President".
GIVEN `declared by Presidential order` IS A BOOLEAN, `exercising side by side in fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the forces are serving together` IF
    `declared by Presidential order`
